  "document": {
    "version": 1,
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "case-intro",
        "type": "comment",
        "position": {
          "x": -520.0,
          "y": -360.0
        },
        "data": {
          "text": "# The Emergence of Reproducibility and Generalizability in Diffusion Models\n\n**Same initialization, different training seeds.** This `small` template contains the complete two-endpoint CIFAR-10 DDPM workflow without checkpoints, loss histories, generated images, or observable results.\n\nThe editable default is the 4,096-sample / 5k-step smoke setting. To reproduce the five-condition study, change the CIFAR-10 `trainSize` to 512, 4,096, or 32,768 and set both trainers to the matching step budget. Train seed 0 and seed 1 from the shared initialization, save both checkpoints, sample with the shared noise seed, then run paired similarity, RP, and nearest-train GL."
        },
        "style": {
          "width": 760
        },
        "parentId": null,
        "extent": null,
        "hidden": null
      },
      {
        "id": "historical-evidence",
        "type": "comment",
        "position": {
          "x": 1430.0,
          "y": -360.0
        },
        "data": {
          "text": "# Protocol\n\nHold the dataset subset, model initialization, optimizer hyperparameters, and sampler noise fixed. Only the trainer seed differs: endpoint A is seed 0 and endpoint B is seed 1. This template is intentionally asset-free; see `docs/reproductions/diffusion-reproducibility.md` for the five historical runs."
        },
        "style": {
          "width": 540
        },
        "parentId": null,
        "extent": null,
        "hidden": null
      },
